= Media Strategy

The media landscape is fractured: cable, podcasts, influencers, and algorithms all pull voters in different directions.

- @local_news: Invest in local outreach
- @influencer_network: Build an influencer and podcast network
- @attack_ads: Go negative on the opposition
- @easy_discard

@local_news
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; rural_dem += 2*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); press_freedom += 1; polarization -= 0.5; month_actions += 1

We back local-news partnerships and town halls, reaching voters who tune out national shouting matches.

@influencer_network
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; young_dem += 5*(1-dissent); working_dem += 1*(1-dissent); educated_dem += 1*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

Friendly creators and podcasters carry our message in their own voices.

@attack_ads
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; suburban_gop -= 3; trump_urgency += 0.3; polarization += 1; gop_enthusiasm += 0.4; month_actions += 1

Contrast ads hit hard, and the other side is energized too.
